1
00:00:02,760 --> 00:00:03,840
Oh, hey, Joey.

2
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:07,900
- Hey. - Listen, I need to ask you something.

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,300
You know how my stepdad's in prison?

4
00:00:11,194 --> 00:00:13,094
- Yeah. - Yeah.

5
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:15,100
He was supposed to get a weekend furlough

6
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,260
so he could go to the wedding.

7
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,900
But he just called and....

8
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:22,200
Well, apparently stabbing lceman in the exercise yard

9
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:23,400
couldn't wait till Monday.

10
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,380
- So he can't come? - No.

11
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,040
And so there's no one

12
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:29,120
to walk me down the aisle.

13
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:30,540
And....

14
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:33,400
Well, I would just really love it if you would do it.

15
00:00:34,989 --> 00:00:36,419
- Seriously? - Yeah.

16
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:39,020
You've, you know, sort of been like a dad to me.

17
00:00:41,140 --> 00:00:42,460
I mean, you've always, you know,

18
00:00:42,540 --> 00:00:44,500
looked out for me and shared your wisdom.

19
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,360
I am pretty "wisdomous."

20
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:52,680
So, what do you say?

21
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,740
Are you kidding? Phoebe, I would be honored.

22
00:00:57,680 --> 00:00:59,160
Oh, thank you.

23
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:03,150
I hope....

24
00:01:04,060 --> 00:01:05,920
I hope you know how much you mean to me.

25
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:08,000
Listen, I hope....

26
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,760
I hope that you know....

27
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:15,405
I don't want you to see your father cry.

28
00:01:15,425 --> 00:01:16,775
Go to your room!

29
00:01:18,981 --> 00:01:21,161
《老友记》第十季第十二集 菲比的婚礼

30
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:11,000
Oh, no, no, no. Let your dad get this.

31
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,700
It's my wedding planner.

32
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:19,360
She's driving me crazy!

33
00:02:20,243 --> 00:02:24,123
Hello? Okay, stop screaming!

34
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,760
Okay, so halibut.

35
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:29,200
All right, so salmon.

36
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:30,560
Either way. I don't--

37
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:31,880
It doesn't matter to me.

38
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,620
Well, it matters to me!

39
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:38,140
Well, I don't care. So you pick.

40
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:39,920
Did you just hang up on me?

41
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:42,400
All right, look,

42
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,660
I need you at the rehearsal dinner

43
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:45,240
tonight at 1800 hours.

44
00:02:45,780 --> 00:02:47,300
Okay. What time is that?

45
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,580
You don't know military time?

46
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,720
military time:24小时制

47
00:02:51,080 --> 00:02:52,880
I must have been in missile training the day

48
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:53,500
they taught that.

49
00:02:55,540 --> 00:02:56,820
Just subtract 12.

50
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,900
Okay, so 1800 minus 12...

51
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:00,680
...is 1788.

52
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:03,340
- Six o'clock! - Okay.

53
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,940
Hold on. Yeah? Geller here.

54
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,620
No, I said it has to be there by 4:00.

55
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:10,990
Goodbye.

56
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:13,600
God. How hard is it to make an ice sculpture?

57
00:03:13,620 --> 00:03:15,940
Wait. Ice sculpture? That sounds really fancy.

58
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:17,980
I told you, I just want a simple wedding.

59
00:03:18,117 --> 00:03:19,580
Please, honey,

60
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,280
leave the details to me.

61
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:22,360
Now, I wanna make this day

62
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,840
as special for you as I can.

63
00:03:24,340 --> 00:03:26,000
I was thinking the harpist

64
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:26,660
should wear white.

65
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:27,440
Harpist?

66
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,460
My friend Marjorie is playing the steel drums.

67
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,360
Oh, she backed out.

68
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:32,700
She did? Why?

69
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:34,140
I made her.

70
00:03:35,200 --> 00:03:37,280
Steel drums don't really say "elegant wedding."

71
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:39,360
Nor does Marjorie's overwhelming scent.

72
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:40,580
Hey!

73
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:43,360
She will shower when Tibet is free.

74
00:03:52,740 --> 00:03:55,780
- Hey. You look great. - You too.

75
00:03:56,220 --> 00:03:58,040
I'm glad we're having a rehearsal dinner.

76
00:03:58,340 --> 00:04:00,000
I rarely practice my meals

77
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:00,700
before I eat.

78
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:04,700
What did we say was your one gift to us?

79
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:05,880
No stupid jokes,

80
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:08,360
but I thought that was for the actual wedding.

81
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:09,260
Rehearse it.

82
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,270
Hi.

83
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:13,820
Thanks for coming, you guys.

84
00:04:13,820 --> 00:04:14,460
Oh, yeah--

85
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:18,540
I was.... I was going for a handshake.

86
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,580
That why your hand's against my crotch?

87
00:04:20,720 --> 00:04:21,880
- That is why. - Yeah.

88
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:25,900
So, Rach, where's Emma?

89
00:04:26,420 --> 00:04:27,760
Monica made me send her to my mom's.

90
00:04:28,280 --> 00:04:30,280
Apparently, babies and weddings don't mix.

91
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:33,360
Are you still crying about your damn baby?

92
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:37,120
Pheebs, you got to keep the line moving.

93
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:38,980
Remember, 20 seconds per person.

94
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,840
You see these clowns all the time.

95
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:46,340
Hey, you're Mike's parents, right?

96
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:47,320
Yes, we are.

97
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:49,020
Our little ones are

98
00:04:49,020 --> 00:04:50,280
growing up fast, aren't they?

99
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:53,840
- How's that? - You know...

100
00:04:53,890 --> 00:04:55,300
...on one hand, you're happy for them.

101
00:04:55,320 --> 00:04:56,820
On the other, it's hard to let go.

102
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,860
Who in God's name are you?

103
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:03,680
I'm not that fond of you either, buddy.

104
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,060
I'm just trying to be nice for the kids.

105
00:05:08,420 --> 00:05:09,560
You know what I realized?

106
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:12,420
We have no idea what we're doing in the wedding tomorrow.

107
00:05:12,860 --> 00:05:14,120
Yeah, I thought we'd be groomsmen.

108
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:15,840
They would have asked us by now.

109
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,860
When did they ask you to be a bridesmaid?

110
00:05:18,793 --> 00:05:20,083
November.

111
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,860
I wanna say it's not looking good.

112
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,420
- Hey, Pheebs? - Sorry?

113
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:26,380
You haven't told these guys

114
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:27,660
what they're doing in the wedding yet.

115
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:31,240
Well, they're not in the wedding.

116
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:32,020
What?

117
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:38,100
Well...

118
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,540
...this is really awkward.

119
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:43,480
Oh, and I can leave.

120
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:47,080
I'm sorry, you guys.

121
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,620
But Mike's got his brother

122
00:05:48,620 --> 00:05:50,100
and his friends from school.

123
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:52,120
So, you know, you were....

124
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:53,120
If it helps,

125
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:54,200
you were next in line.

126
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,840
You just missed the cut.

127
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:57,900
Oh, man.

128
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:00,720
This is like figure skating team all over again.

129
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:04,440
figure skating/synchronized swimming/balance beam:均为女子运动项目

130
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:05,560
I mean, synchronized swimming.

131
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:09,000
I mean-- I mean, the balance beam.

132
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:11,400
- Help me. - Football.

133
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:12,720
Thank you.

134
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:15,940
Oh, Pheebs, spit that out. That has pork in it.

135
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:20,000
I thought the pot stickers were supposed to be vegetarian?

136
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:21,820
Yeah, I changed them.

137
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,680
I sent you a fax about it.

138
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:25,760
I don't have a fax machine.

139
00:06:27,980 --> 00:06:29,540
Well, then there are gonna be a few surprises.

140
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,800
I can't believe we're gonna be

141
00:06:33,800 --> 00:06:36,000
the only people that aren't in this wedding.

142
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,960
I know. I hate being left out of things.

143
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:38,940
And it's a wedding.

144
00:06:39,780 --> 00:06:41,380
It'll be weird if I'm not in it.

145
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:45,900
- Hey, guys, how's it going? - Fine.

146
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:48,080
We're sitting here, alone, doing nothing.

147
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:50,460
It's our rehearsal for tomorrow.

148
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:54,640
Look, about tomorrow, I've got a question for you.

149
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:56,840
I found out one of my groomsmen had an emergency

150
00:06:56,840 --> 00:06:57,740
and can't make it.

151
00:06:57,980 --> 00:06:58,540
What happened?

152
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,620
Who cares? And...?

153
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:04,040
And I was wondering if one of you guys--

154
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,440
- I'll do it! -No... Me!

155
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:08,120
You both wanna do it?

156
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:09,580
There's only room for one.

157
00:07:09,680 --> 00:07:11,300
Pick me. I look great in a tux,

158
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,580
and I won't steal focus.

159
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:13,180
No, Mike.

160
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:16,080
No, no, you wanna pick me. I mean.... Watch.

161
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:24,640
You know, I really don't feel very comfortable

162
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:25,660
making this decision.

163
00:07:25,970 --> 00:07:27,020
You know, Phoebe knows you better.

164
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:28,140
I'm gonna let her choose.

165
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:31,860
Well, if Phoebe's choosing,

166
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:34,460
then say hello to Mike's next groomsman.

167
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,260
Oh, I will. But I will need a mirror...

168
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:40,160
...as he is me.

169
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:44,080
Please. You're going down.

170
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:45,320
You are going "downer."

171
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,700
They say that on the figure skating team?

172
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:49,600
I wouldn't know. I didn't make it.

173
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:56,520
You know I'm filling in for Phoebe's stepdad tomorrow,

174
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:56,960
right?

175
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:58,460
Yeah. Yeah. Hey, thanks for doing that.

176
00:07:58,460 --> 00:07:59,800
Oh, hey, my pleasure.

177
00:08:00,300 --> 00:08:02,320
So, what are your intentions with my Phoebe?

178
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:07,100
- I intend to marry her. - Oh, a wiseacre.

179
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:11,180
I understand you plan to support your wife

180
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,820
by playing the piano?

181
00:08:14,580 --> 00:08:15,640
Isn't that kind of unstable?

182
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,200
- No more so than acting. - Strike two.

183
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:24,180
You're right. She probably will support me.

184
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,820
Hey, unless we move in with you, Dad.

185
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:28,700
Strike three.

186
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,840
You only get one more, Mike.

187
00:08:35,700 --> 00:08:37,720
So? What did you decide?

188
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,820
I decided to pee.

189
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:42,920
He didn't tell you?

190
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:44,100
You have to choose one of us

191
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:44,820
to be in your wedding.

192
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:46,160
One of the groomsmen fell out.

193
00:08:46,220 --> 00:08:47,360
Oh, no, no.

194
00:08:47,460 --> 00:08:49,140
I can't choose between you two.

195
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:50,820
I love you both so much.

196
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:52,200
Just not enough to put us in

197
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:53,640
the original wedding party.

198
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:57,220
But I don't wanna choose. It's....

199
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:58,440
Okay, wait. Rach?

200
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:03,160
Listen, I have a very special bridesmaid task for you to do.

201
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,080
Goody! What is it?

202
00:09:05,740 --> 00:09:08,180
Well, there's a spot open for only one groomsman...

203
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:10,280
...and you have to choose between Ross and Chandler.

204
00:09:10,340 --> 00:09:11,320
So good luck with that.

205
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:13,180
What? What, what, what?

206
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,540
No, I don't wanna do that.

207
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:16,700
All right. I guess I have to find a new bridesmaid.

208
00:09:16,780 --> 00:09:17,600
I'll do it!

209
00:09:19,160 --> 00:09:20,960
Okay, it's 2100 hours.

210
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,140
Time for your toast.

211
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:23,740
Do I have time to go to the bathroom?

212
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:25,560
You had a bathroom break at 2030.

213
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:27,360
Pee on your own time, Mike.

214
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,340
In regards to the toasts, okay,

215
00:09:32,380 --> 00:09:33,600
you wanna keep them short.

216
00:09:33,860 --> 00:09:35,100
Nothing kills a rehearsal dinner

217
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:36,700
like long speeches. Okay.

218
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:38,840
You just get in, do your thing, and get out.

219
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:40,460
Is that what you say to Chandler?

220
00:09:43,017 --> 00:09:44,497
It's 2101,

221
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:45,340
and I am not amused.

222
00:09:47,063 --> 00:09:48,123
Okay.

223
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:51,660
The bride and groom have a few words they'd like to say.

224
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,600
Okay. Hello, everyone.

225
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:58,860
And thank you all for being here tonight.

226
00:09:59,560 --> 00:10:01,000
So tomorrow's the big event.

227
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:02,700
Some of you might not know,

228
00:10:02,860 --> 00:10:05,120
but Mike and I didn't get off to the best start.

229
00:10:06,060 --> 00:10:09,080
Yeah. My friend Joey and l...

230
00:10:09,640 --> 00:10:12,740
...decided to fix each other up with friends. So l--

231
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:16,880
Oh, okay. I....

232
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:19,940
I gave it a lot of thought,

233
00:10:19,940 --> 00:10:21,960
and I fixed him up with my friend Mary Ellen...

234
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:24,260
...who couldn't be here tonight, because.... It's not--

235
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:27,540
It's not important. Well, she's in rehab.

236
00:10:29,606 --> 00:10:30,556
Anyway.

237
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:33,700
So Joey said that he was fixing me up with his friend Mike...

238
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,200
...only he didn't have a friend Mike,

239
00:10:35,540 --> 00:10:37,560
so he just brought my Mike.

240
00:10:37,560 --> 00:10:39,120
And-- And--

241
00:10:40,260 --> 00:10:43,140
But despite, you know-- It got good.

242
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:46,640
Ok, I wanna take a moment

243
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:47,880
to mention my mother,

244
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:49,320
who couldn't be here.

245
00:10:49,320 --> 00:10:50,510
Oh, God.

246
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:53,230
And.... And moment's over.

247
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:56,040
So okay.... Oh, no, forget that.

248
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:58,460
I can forget that. Oh, this is funny.

249
00:10:58,840 --> 00:11:02,580
Oh, but you need to know that to get that.

250
00:11:02,760 --> 00:11:04,440
So.... Oh, well, okay.

251
00:11:05,454 --> 00:11:07,884
I.... Okay.

252
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:10,280
Okay, Monica, I can't do it like this!

253
00:11:12,020 --> 00:11:14,160
This is my wedding, okay?

254
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:16,060
I don't want this--

255
00:11:16,060 --> 00:11:18,500
Or this-- Or this--

256
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:20,960
Okay? I just wanted a simple wedding...

257
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:22,840
...where my fiance can go to the bathroom

258
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:24,180
any time he wants!

259
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:30,080
- You know what? You're done. - What?

260
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:31,080
You're fired!

261
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:34,120
Cheers.

262
00:11:45,377 --> 00:11:47,077
- Hey. - Happy wedding day.

263
00:11:47,163 --> 00:11:48,843
Happy my wedding day to you.

264
00:11:50,132 --> 00:11:51,252
Joey, listen,

265
00:11:51,326 --> 00:11:52,556
this is gonna be bridesmaid central,

266
00:11:52,632 --> 00:11:53,142
all right?

267
00:11:53,204 --> 00:11:54,294
We're gonna have hair and makeup

268
00:11:54,367 --> 00:11:55,427
in the bathroom.

269
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:56,820
I had to move a couple things in the fridge

270
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:58,060
to make room for the corsages.

271
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:01,450
因为瑞秋说要把corsage放到冰箱里  乔伊以为可以吃

272
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,920
Man! I wouldn't have had breakfast

273
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:02,560
if I knew there was gonna be corsages.

274
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:07,940
Hi.

275
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:10,540
About last night....

276
00:12:11,800 --> 00:12:13,980
I know you're under a lot of stress, and....

277
00:12:14,920 --> 00:12:17,760
Well, even though the things you said

278
00:12:17,922 --> 00:12:19,722
...as someone who's never been fired before--

279
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:21,420
My point is....

280
00:12:21,440 --> 00:12:24,620
Well, I'm willing to take my job back.

281
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,420
Oh, well, that's okay.

282
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,100
I think you and I will do much better

283
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:33,000
if you're just here as a bridesmaid.

284
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:36,320
Is that so?

285
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:38,360
Okay.

286
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:40,400
If that's really what you want,

287
00:12:40,400 --> 00:12:41,060
then here.

288
00:12:41,540 --> 00:12:42,700
I give you the headset.

289
00:12:43,540 --> 00:12:44,700
I don't really wanna give you the headset.

290
00:12:46,460 --> 00:12:47,340
I guess if you're taking over,

291
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:50,140
then you should probably return these messages.

292
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:52,040
Wow. This is a lot.

293
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:54,540
But I'm sure you can handle this.

294
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:56,120
I have won awards...

295
00:12:56,120 --> 00:12:57,580
...for my organizational skills.

296
00:12:57,620 --> 00:12:59,260
But I'm sure you'll do fine.

297
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,340
You've won awards?

298
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:02,180
I printed them out on my computer.

299
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,160
- Hey. - Hi.

300
00:13:06,335 --> 00:13:07,380
Where's Rach?

301
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:08,340
She's in her room. Why?

302
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:09,340
I have to talk to her about

303
00:13:09,340 --> 00:13:11,000
this groomsman situation.

304
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,900
Ok, I'm not gonna watch Chandler up there

305
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:14,740
while I'm in the seats like some chump.

306
00:13:20,400 --> 00:13:22,540
My God, you're breathtaking.

307
00:13:26,060 --> 00:13:26,720
What do you want?

308
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:29,500
You haven't by any chance

309
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:31,340
chosen a groomsman yet, have you?

310
00:13:31,758 --> 00:13:32,538
Ross,

311
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:34,700
please don't make this harder than it already is.

312
00:13:34,840 --> 00:13:35,400
I'm not.

313
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:37,140
I'm making it easier. Pick me.

314
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,000
Chandler said it's important to him too.

315
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:42,160
Listen. Listen.

316
00:13:42,300 --> 00:13:43,660
Whoever you pick

317
00:13:43,660 --> 00:13:45,860
is gonna walk down the aisle with you.

318
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:48,700
Now, I promise I won't say a word.

319
00:13:48,700 --> 00:13:50,000
But if you pick Chandler...

320
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,540
...he's gonna be whispering stupid jokes

321
00:13:51,540 --> 00:13:52,820
in your ear the whole time.

322
00:13:54,440 --> 00:13:56,500
Oh, you are the lesser of two evils.

323
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:57,020
Yes!

324
00:14:03,580 --> 00:14:05,520
Sven, I don't understand what you're saying.

325
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:07,240
What is wrong with the flowers?

326
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:09,860
"Lorkins"? What the hell are "lorkins"?

327
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:10,660
I know.

328
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:13,540
Hey.

329
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,200
Mike, if you were Swedish...

330
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:18,300
...and you were saying the word "lorkins," what flower would that be?

331
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:19,880
Orchids?

332
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:20,760
Right there!

333
00:14:20,940 --> 00:14:22,720
That's why I'm marrying you.

334
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:31,300
Hello, Michael.

335
00:14:33,340 --> 00:14:33,960
Joseph.

336
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:37,900
May I have a word with you, please?

337
00:14:49,129 --> 00:14:50,419
This is...

338
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:51,600
...great.

339
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:53,940
Have a seat.

340
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,020
Last night...

341
00:15:00,580 --> 00:15:03,300
...l tried to welcome you into my family.

342
00:15:05,629 --> 00:15:08,879
And instead, you disrespect me.

343
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:11,480
I cannot allow this.

344
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:15,380
Are you rehearsing for some really bad Mafia movie?

345
00:15:16,900 --> 00:15:18,060
More back talk.

346
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,180
And yes,

347
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:22,240
I may be borrowing a few lines

348
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:24,640
from my recent unsuccessful audition...

349
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,300
...for <i>Family Honor 2:</i>

350
00:15:26,380 --> 00:15:27,500
<i>This A-Time It's A-Personal.</i>

351
00:15:30,980 --> 00:15:32,940
Joey, I kind of have a lot to do today.

352
00:15:33,320 --> 00:15:33,740
What do you want?

353
00:15:33,760 --> 00:15:35,420
I want you to take this seriously!

354
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,320
Phoebe is very,

355
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:39,360
very important to me, okay?

356
00:15:39,560 --> 00:15:40,080
I wanna make sure

357
00:15:40,260 --> 00:15:41,880
you are gonna take care of her.

358
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:45,260
Joe, I love Phoebe.

359
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:48,240
She's the most important thing in my life.

360
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:50,860
I'd die before I let anything happen to her.

361
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:55,080
That's what I wanted to hear.

362
00:15:56,640 --> 00:15:59,140
Because she's family, okay?

363
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:00,640
And now you're gonna be family.

364
00:16:01,400 --> 00:16:02,700
And there's nothing more important

365
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:05,220
in the whole world than family.

366
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:08,460
That must have been one lousy movie.

367
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:09,840
That was me!

368
00:16:13,964 --> 00:16:14,914
Hi.

369
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:16,400
Let's talk about this groomsman thing.

370
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:17,540
If you pick Ross,

371
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:19,400
he'll walk you down the aisle just fine.

372
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:21,260
But if you choose me...

373
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:23,280
...you'll be getting some comedy.

374
00:16:26,514 --> 00:16:28,614
Even so...

375
00:16:32,140 --> 00:16:33,880
...l think I'm gonna pick Ross.

376
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:35,740
Let me tell you why you need to pick me.

377
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,180
See, when I was a kid, you know,

378
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:42,740
I was always left out of everything...

379
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:46,140
You know... and it really made me feel insecure.

380
00:16:46,900 --> 00:16:50,060
I was always picked last in gym...

381
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:53,100
...even behind that fat exchange student

382
00:16:53,100 --> 00:16:54,820
who didn't know the rules to baseball.

383
00:16:55,320 --> 00:16:56,980
I mean, this guy would strike out

384
00:16:56,980 --> 00:16:57,920
and then run to third.

385
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,360
Anyway, if I'm the only one

386
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:04,360
left out of this wedding...

387
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:05,960
...l just know that all those feelings

388
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:07,520
are gonna come rushing back.

389
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,760
All right, fine, I pick you.

390
00:17:12,780 --> 00:17:13,540
Yes!

391
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:17,900
Make "groom" for Chandler.

392
00:17:15,640 --> 00:17:18,730
groom与room谐音 钱德勒做了"伴郎"亦即有了"一席之地"

393
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:23,200
Oh, my.

394
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:27,400
No, we're gonna do it my way.

395
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:29,440
Because your way is stupid.

396
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:31,380
All right, I got to go.

397
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:32,580
I have another call, Reverend.

398
00:17:35,300 --> 00:17:35,700
Hello?

399
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:38,020
I'm glad we had this little talk.

400
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:38,800
Yes.

401
00:17:39,280 --> 00:17:40,960
And thanks for all the wedding night advice.

402
00:17:42,400 --> 00:17:44,120
That didn't make me uncomfortable at all.

403
00:17:45,080 --> 00:17:47,020
All right, so I'll see everybody tonight.

404
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:48,300
- Okay. - Bye.

405
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,320
Did you guys know that

406
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:56,200
there's a giant ice sculpture in the hall?

407
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:59,180
Oh, my God, what's it doing here?

408
00:17:59,530 --> 00:18:01,360
I guess it got sent to the billing address

409
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:02,980
as opposed to the shipping address.

410
00:18:03,680 --> 00:18:04,280
What a pickle.

411
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:07,780
Oh, my God, everything's such a mess.

412
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:09,760
Why is this happening to me?

413
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:13,080
How bad do you wanna stick your tongue on that?

414
00:18:20,580 --> 00:18:22,420
- How's it going? - Good.

415
00:18:23,080 --> 00:18:24,920
I'm just getting some coffee

416
00:18:25,500 --> 00:18:26,700
so I'm alert for the wedding.

417
00:18:28,420 --> 00:18:30,120
That's what I was doing too.

418
00:18:31,302 --> 00:18:34,220
Well, you have fun tonight.

419
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:35,960
- You too. - Oh, I will.

420
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:38,460
Me too.

421
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:43,620
Wait a minute.

422
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:45,460
I know why I'm being such an ass.

423
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:46,120
Why are you?

424
00:18:47,840 --> 00:18:49,220
I'm not supposed to tell you.

425
00:18:49,300 --> 00:18:50,880
I'm not supposed to tell you.

426
00:18:51,840 --> 00:18:53,640
You told us both we could be in the wedding?

427
00:18:56,080 --> 00:18:57,240
In my defense,

428
00:18:57,360 --> 00:18:59,260
you weren't supposed to tell each other!

429
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:02,000
Rachel, only one of us can do it.

430
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:03,120
You have to choose.

431
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:05,140
You and me together again.

432
00:19:07,220 --> 00:19:07,880
Rach, Rach?

433
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:08,520
Knock-knock.

434
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:10,640
- Who's there? - I'll tell you at the wedding.

435
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:13,520
Hey, I forgot my scarf.

436
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:15,760
You know what. I can't do this.

437
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:17,400
I don't know which one of you guys to pick.

438
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:18,680
Oh, you haven't picked yet?

439
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:20,640
Oh, good, because I had an idea.

440
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:21,840
I thought it would be fun

441
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:24,560
if the third groomsman was my family dog, Chappy.

442
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:26,880
What? A dog?

443
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:29,100
No. Rachel gets to choose.

444
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:31,960
Wow, this is a tough one.

445
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:34,440
I think I'm gonna have to go with the dog.

446
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,560
So, what you're saying is that

447
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:40,200
the chef is at the Hamilton Club...

448
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:41,260
...but the food is not?

449
00:19:41,260 --> 00:19:42,640
And the drinks are there

450
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,060
but the bartender is not?

451
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:47,740
Are you freaking kidding me?

452
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:49,120
How's it going?

453
00:19:50,620 --> 00:19:51,960
- Help me. - What?

454
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:54,240
I want you to be crazy bitch again.

455
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:57,760
Really?

456
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:00,320
Please?

457
00:20:01,660 --> 00:20:03,220
You really want me to come back?

458
00:20:03,340 --> 00:20:05,000
More than I wanna get married.

459
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:10,260
Okay, people, we are back in business!

460
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:15,140
Oh, God, I have missed you so much. Okay.

461
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:16,780
Ok. Get your hair and makeup done.

462
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:18,200
I'll take care of everything.

463
00:20:18,340 --> 00:20:19,660
Hey, what are you guys gonna do?

464
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:20,820
About what?

465
00:20:20,980 --> 00:20:23,580
The blizzard. I just saw on the news...

466
00:20:23,580 --> 00:20:25,440
...it's the worst snowstorm in 20 years.

467
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,140
They already closed all the bridges and tunnels.

468
00:20:29,280 --> 00:20:30,640
But the band and the photographer

469
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,100
are coming in from New Jersey.

470
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:33,640
I don't think they are.

471
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:36,660
Looks like you're not gonna

472
00:20:36,660 --> 00:20:37,820
be in the wedding, either.

473
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:40,940
So sorry, Pheebs.

474
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:55,380
Well, the club lost its power.

475
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:57,500
Yeah according to the news, most of the city did.

476
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,400
Since when do you watch the news?

477
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:01,000
For your information...

478
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:03,360
...since they hired a very hot weather girl.

479
00:21:05,300 --> 00:21:06,000
I can't believe

480
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,860
you aren't getting married today.

481
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:08,720
I know.

482
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:12,220
Wow, you know, it's so beautiful out there.

483
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:14,120
You always wanted to get married outside.

484
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,840
Why don't you just do it on the street?

485
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:16,600
What?

486
00:21:16,860 --> 00:21:18,800
Well, look, it's hardly snowing anymore.

487
00:21:19,750 --> 00:21:22,640
I mean, you couldn't ask for a more romantic setting.

488
00:21:23,120 --> 00:21:24,380
This could be the simple wedding

489
00:21:24,380 --> 00:21:25,220
you've always wanted.

490
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,020
What do you think?

491
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:31,880
I think I wanna get married to you today.

492
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:37,660
Me too. Monica, do you think we could do it?

493
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:40,860
Affirmative!

494
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:51,420
Okay, let's get these chairs out here!

495
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:53,520
Gunther, hit the Christmas lights.

496
00:22:01,360 --> 00:22:04,420
Okay, who left the ice sculpture

497
00:22:04,420 --> 00:22:05,980
on the steam grate?

498
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:08,860
Michael.

499
00:22:09,300 --> 00:22:11,680
Hey, you made it. Great. Chappy!

500
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:14,200
- There you go. - Hi. Hi.

501
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:17,860
Mom, I know getting married in the street isn't

502
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:18,900
what you approve of.

503
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,660
No, it's lovely.

504
00:22:20,840 --> 00:22:22,600
The lights and the snow.

505
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,280
I could look at them forever.

506
00:22:24,920 --> 00:22:26,320
I crushed a pill and put it in her drink.

507
00:22:28,280 --> 00:22:28,940
Come on, sweetheart.

508
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:33,240
You know, Chappy's too small

509
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:34,420
to handle all this snow.

510
00:22:34,520 --> 00:22:36,160
Someone has to walk him down the aisle.

511
00:22:37,320 --> 00:22:38,280
Would this person be in the wedding?

512
00:22:38,620 --> 00:22:39,020
I guess.

513
00:22:39,240 --> 00:22:40,352
- I'll do it! - I'll do it!

514
00:22:40,372 --> 00:22:42,220
Chandler, hello?

515
00:22:42,240 --> 00:22:44,680
I mean, aren't you scared of dogs?

516
00:22:44,860 --> 00:22:45,680
I'm not scared.

517
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:47,780
I'll just take little Chappy and--

518
00:22:47,780 --> 00:22:48,560
He can sense my fear!

519
00:22:48,620 --> 00:22:49,480
My throat is exposed!

520
00:22:52,320 --> 00:22:54,460
I guess I'm in the wedding then.

521
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:57,300
He stinks.

522
00:22:58,860 --> 00:22:59,860
Level one alert!

523
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:02,340
I repeat, level one, this is not a drill!

524
00:23:02,460 --> 00:23:03,640
We have a situation.

525
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:04,540
The minister called.

526
00:23:04,560 --> 00:23:05,860
He's snowed in, he can't make it.

527
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,900
- Oh, no. - Hey, don't worry.

528
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:09,220
I'm still ordained from your wedding.

529
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:10,020
Really?

530
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:12,300
Yeah. You think I'd give up being a minister

531
00:23:12,340 --> 00:23:13,640
and pay to ride the subway?

532
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:17,880
Ministers don't ride the subway for free.

533
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,820
I had to read the Bible pretty carefully,

534
00:23:19,860 --> 00:23:21,180
but, yeah, we do.

535
00:23:22,540 --> 00:23:23,920
Ok, if Joey does the ceremony,

536
00:23:23,980 --> 00:23:25,940
then we have to find someone else to walk Phoebe down the aisle.

537
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:26,500
I'll do it!

538
00:23:32,100 --> 00:23:33,720
Okay, Mike and Joey, get in position.

539
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,300
Chandler, come with me.

540
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,400
Okay, Joey's doing the ceremony,

541
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:45,900
and Chandler's giving you away.

542
00:23:46,460 --> 00:23:48,480
Oh, okay. Hi, new Dad.

543
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:53,540
So you ready to do this?

544
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:56,260
Oh, my God. This is really happening.

545
00:23:58,120 --> 00:24:00,220
